The search results confirm that the Mercedes-Benz 500 SEC (C126) was produced from 1980/1982 to 1991 (Source 1, 3, 5, 7, 14). It was a coupe based on the W126 S-Class sedan of that era (Source 1, 7, 11). Mercedes-Benz has since changed its naming conventions, and there is no current model referred to as the "most recent version" of the 500 SEC. The S-Class Coupe existed in later generations (like the C140 and C217), but the "500 SEC" designation specifically belongs to the vintage C126 model.

Since the requested model ("most recent version of Mercedes-Benz 500 SEC") does not correspond to a specific, currently produced vehicle in today's market, the data is ambiguous for the purpose of scoring against current benchmarks.

